1. The generated data in data/ is derived from the keyword and help data under
   server/data/. It is transformed into the shapes described in README.md; no
   upstream source code is copied into it. provenance.json records the upstream
   commit each published data set came from.

2. The language server in server/ is the upstream server compiled from source at
   that same commit, because upstream publishes no built artifact: its dist/ is
   ignored and it has no release assets. The build is reproducible in content but
   not byte for byte, as the upstream typeshed loader inlines the Python stubs in
   filesystem order rather than sorting them.

